= Human Factors Concept  [HFC-nn] =

//A specific principle or finding from human-factors literature, selected because it explains something in this Problem.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. HFC-01, HFC-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained — direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant — flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Measure or Evaluation Method, cite existing use in a validation study or authoritative literature (e.g. a validated-instrument source or textbook) instead.
|Concept statement|the principle, stated so a reader unfamiliar with the literature can use it.
|Human factor addressed|the underlying phenomenon (trust, workload, situation awareness, stigma, behaviour change…).
|Proposed mechanism|what causes what, and under what conditions — this is what makes an expected effect predictable rather than hoped for.
|Source|specific citation, not a keyword or a field name.
|Conditions and population of validity|where the finding holds, and any known limits on transferring it to this Stakeholder group.
|Predicted Effect type|what kind of effect this concept would lead you to expect.
|Associated Measures|Measure ID(s) that could detect that effect.

== Graph edges ==

grounds → (Specification-phase) Claim; explains → Human Value.